  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The rehearsal includes one planned break within the booked duration, and singers may also step out briefly for personal needs.\", \"decision\": \"How should the main rehearsal break be timed?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe conductor places the planned break at a fixed clock time and includes it in the rehearsal notice. Singers can anticipate the rest period, and musical work must be organized around an already visible stopping point.\nThe conductor announces a short break window at the start and chooses a natural stopping point within it. Singers know roughly when rest is coming while the final timing can follow the progress of the rehearsal.\nThe conductor places the planned break after a named rehearsal block and announces that position at the start. The pause follows a coherent piece of musical work while remaining predictable within the published rehearsal sequence."
    }
  ],
